Package: monitoreo
Type: Package
Title: Satellite Variables of MonitorEO (OBSNEV) with Google Earth Engine
Version: 0.3.4
Authors@R: person("OBSNEV - Universidad de Granada", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "javier.martinez@ugr.es")
Description: MonitorEO-OBSNEV is an open monitoring tool of Essential Biodiversity Variables based on satellite
    sensors and models generated by the University of Granada. It enables citizens, managers, and scientists
    to create maps and graphs of key ecosystem metrics to support decision-making.
    Time series, maps, statistics and exports to Google Drive of the variables of the MonitorEO app
    (NDVI, EVI, NDWI, LSWI, NDSI, albedo, land surface temperature, evapotranspiration, LAI, ...) of
    Sentinel-2, Landsat and MODIS, with its pixel filters, computed with Google Earth Engine through the
    Python package 'monitoreo' (the same functions as its QGIS plugin and its MCP server). Earth Engine
    images can be shown with 'rgee'.
License: GPL (>= 3)
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.0)
Imports: reticulate (>= 1.30), jsonlite
Suggests: rgee, ggplot2, leaflet, sf, testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
